{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex","id":747745,"title":"Can the God Machine be the Apex?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-01T16:31:07-08:00","id":747745,"title":"Can the God Machine be the Apex?","content":"so... I'm sure the God Machine doesn't have projects everywhere, but if it does it seems like it would be the most powerful supernatural.<br /> <br /> perhaps the problem is the term &quot;powerful&quot; I get a secondary feeling from this section that power has nothing to do with it. Rather visibility, the most &quot;seen&quot; supernatural, the thing that is haunting the most people's dreams.<br /> <br /> More thought, would the Prince be the Apex? or the Prince's Hound who is probably more often observed conducting unsavory behavior<br /> <br /> Maybe I should put these comments in the errata thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 11-01-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:41:40-08:00","id":747787,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine is dispassionate, secretive, a consummate liar, incapable of expressing itself without an intermediary, and disinclined to exert more effort than strictly necessary for a project unless doing so allows it to advance multiple agendas in the process.<br /> <br /> The question is also kind of like asking if Australia can be the scariest thing in the Pacific Ocean \u2014 it's simply beyond the scale of consideration. The Machine might engineer something that could go on to become the Apex, but the system of arcane physics itself is only really known by anyone in the abstract sense of a metaphysical umbrella for various conspiracies, cryptids and OOPArts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:07:21-08:00","id":748080,"title":"","content":"What about Angels then? do they count? trying to figure out where the line is, and how best to determine what the real apex creature is, and how and when that changes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:12:05-08:00","id":748092,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine can't be an Apex for a few reasons. The primary one I'm going with is that the God Machine isn't a discrete entity you can point to and say &quot;that's God.&quot; There's a little saying in some of the Abrahamic faiths - &quot;God lives in all of us.&quot; In the WoD, this is literally true - the GM is the sum of all its Infrastructure, cultists, fascilities, and angels. Its like a giant program that's being run simultaneously on different computers across the globe. Every human brain has a tiny part of it devoted to the God-Machine. Every angel is part of its processing capabilities. Every Infrastructure is part of its I/O system. The G-M is baically the Internet meets Skynet.<br /> <br /> Kind of hard to be the Apex of a city when you're more of a phenomenon than a being. Individual angels might qualify, but the G-M is too scattered to make sense as one. <br /> <br /> Also, given that Unchained aren't bound by whatever standard applies to the Dark Mother's Children, it makes little sense for angels and other God-Machine derivitives to apply to the whole Astral thing as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Prince versus the Sheriff question... the Apex is open to interpretation, depending on what rubric you want to use to measure it. Its an entirely subjective concept. Literally. What it means to be an Apex changes from city to city - the Astral reflection of every city is different and weighs things differently, has different standards. For example - we have an alpha wolf, elder vamp, and master mage. In a city dominated by gang violence, the wolf might be the Apex, in a college town the mage might be on top, while a high society area like the Hamptons would favor the vampire as Apex. Same three people, each being the Apex depending on the local culture.<br /> <br /> And that's before we start getting into individual splat politics. A Kindred Prince isn't always the most powerful/smartest/savvy vampire; the guy could be a front, could be ruled jointly by covenant elders, could have been elected by a Carthian assembly, could be any number of things. It all comes down to what makes sense for the themes of your individual story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:27:11-08:00","id":748111,"title":"","content":"I'd say active angels count, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:27:16-08:00","id":748112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every Infrastructure is part of its I/O system. The G-M is baically the Internet meets Skynet. </div> </div> </div> (being a programmer) is the Google search engine a single thing? no, not really, and at the same time yes. I'm not really sure that a &quot;program&quot; working across a large cluster of systems really makes it not a single entity, in the same way that some pieces of software aren't individually useful (the netflix tech blog recently talked about how some of there open source programs aren't individually useful). I'm made up of cells does that make me less of a single entity? just a hard line to draw, I'm not convinced that being a distributed system makes the god machine less of a single entity. That said, I otherwise get the point, and I was also kind of driving at the fact that the GM/Demons aren't really &quot;family&quot; to the Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:32:01-08:00","id":748118,"title":"","content":"I think the question I'm asking with the Prince, if humanity never see's his power, can he still be the Apex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:35:57-08:00","id":748121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748111#post748111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say active angels count, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd held that position up until the Machine was highlighted in all the book's discussion of how demons aren't kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T18:43:22-08:00","id":748160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748121#post748121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd held that position up until the Machine was highlighted in all the book's discussion of how demons aren't kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>right but in the Apex section (or at least what I've read so far) it only says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the most powerful supernatural being in a region, whether or not that being is aware of its influence on<br /> the Primordial Dream or of the Children in general. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:31:39-08:00","id":748230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748160#post748160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">right but in the Apex section (or at least what I've read so far) it only says</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair though the God Machine is doesn't have many beings that can be argued to be anywhere near its level. Which considering the scale the GM effects would just mean all areas would register the GM as the apex then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:48:59-08:00","id":748245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748121#post748121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd held that position up until the Machine was highlighted in all the book's discussion of how demons aren't kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Machine's relationship with the Astral Realms is one of those things I should probably go and dig into. We know It can invade them, but yer right in the deeper implications of that fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:07:05-08:00","id":748269,"title":"","content":"Being Kin with Beasts is not a prerequisite to affect the Astral, and the Primordial Dream therein. The Astral could be called a multiverse on its own, and pretty much all thoughts and ideas shape it to some degree. You just need to be the most feared supernatural in the specific area. That status of top dog is attainable by any splat. The usual approach of Demons as these impostors infiltrating human organizations can be pretty scary, but more in a &quot;holy shit, they could be anywhere and anyone&quot; way, rather than a &quot;I have huge teeth and will eat you alive&quot; way. We even have modern folklore of sorts for monsters like that in the form of Reptilian Aliens and Men In Black. That central concept behind body-snatchers both religious and sci-fi could have originated in ancient times when people developed mental illnesses and acted in ways that were socially unacceptable, but the understanding of the human mind was extremely lacking, so we'd say it wasn't really them, but some <i>Other</i> controlling them. I'd say Demons can tap into enough primal fear to attain Apex status. They even have an Exploit called Rip The Gates, which lets them enter the Astral, but as material beings with the nine standard Attributes.<br /> <br /> Angels, on the other hand, can also be anywhere and anyone, but they are feared more for the divine punishment they might bring if one displeases God enough. They're like the other side of the coin, and have just as much presence in our myths and religions as demonic figures. Fear can be mixed with awe to become a sort of respect, but the methods that can be used to achieve such respect can run the moral spectrum. But this is a horror game we're talking about, not a comfort bringing religion. God-Machine Angels do not hold any divine love for humans unless they Fall, which is one of the main twists present in D:tD. The respect they command is wholly fear-based, regardless of what message they are ordered to send. Without competent Demons to fight the God-Machine, a sufficiently sophisticated Angel can become Apex, and the light it will spread through the Lairs in the area will not be a loving one.<br /> <br /> Besides, asking if the God-Machine can be Apex is like asking if the Abyss or Divine Fire/Principle can be Apex. They aren't characters, they're plot devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-01-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T20:38:42-08:00","id":748305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748269#post748269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Kin with Beasts is not a prerequisite to affect the Astral, and the Primordial Dream therein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinship works on the basis that most supernatural beings draw metaphysical descent from the Dark Mother (who some schools of thought say <i>is</i> the Primordial Dream) and the only ability demons have at the time of this writing that specifically interfaces with the Astral is a) an Exploit (i.e. a weirdo sideways abuse of the systems put in place by the Machine to do things they weren't intended to) and b) an exceedingly temporary gatemaker rather than anything more lasting or sophisticated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just need to be the most feared supernatural in the specific area. That status of top dog is attainable by any splat. </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine operates on parameters of secrecy and precision and regularly employs memory-erasure for those instances in which the aforementioned are insufficient, and the Unchained tend to follow suit in their own endeavors out of plain practicality. These are not the practices of beings poised to go borderline public in the name of becoming the scariest nightmare in the basement even if they were actually capable of presenting a genuine true form instead of an intermediary argument for homunculus theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T21:11:42-08:00","id":748368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748230#post748230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair though the God Machine is doesn't have many beings that can be argued to be anywhere near its level. Which considering the scale the GM effects would just mean all areas would register the GM as the apex then.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I don't think &quot;most powerful&quot; really has anything to do it, even if you simply eliminate GM, Mages, and Angels are generally way more powerful than vampires werewolves. So I'm trying to figure out what the driving factor is.<br /> <br /> I would think that it's the predator that most other predator's in the area fear. Which generally probably eliminates the GM, and Angels which usually probably have no interest in other splats, this actually goes for a lot of splats. It raises the predatory splats (vamps, werewolves) to the top though. This isn't what the passage seems to describe though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 11-02-2015, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T22:09:31-08:00","id":748458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748368#post748368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that it's the predator that most other predator's in the area fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Okay, that bit you quoted earlier?<br /> <br /> Did you bother to read the rest of the paragraph?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The being, however, <b>must have regular, direct contact with humanity.</b> An elder vampire that dwells in an isolated home and has his meals (as it were) delivered by underlings probably doesn\u2019t qualify, because he doesn\u2019t <b>interact with people often enough or in varied enough contexts to become entrenched in the Primordial Dream.</b> A mighty werewolf hunter, though, who leads her pack through the dark alleys of the city hunting her quarry, might have <b>spawned enough nightmares and inadvertently created enough Chambers</b> to become the city\u2019s Apex. </div> </div> </div>The conditions that create a Chamber are on pages 94 and 95. Lingering Chambers stem from encounters with the supernatural traumatic enough to cause actual loss of Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T03:13:05-08:00","id":748830,"title":"","content":"I always assume that Apex is the being that humans <i>unconsciously</i> <i><b>fear </b>most</i> - to be Apex, you need to scar humans most from other monsters. And they need to tell stories one another about your horrific doings.<br /> <br /> So much higher probability to become Apex have vampire Sheriff than a Prince - as undead bodyguard dragging or killing people on the streets is much scarier to general humans population than even the most creepy Nosferatu watching them from the sewers. <i>It's all depends on direct impact the monster do on human minds.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T06:34:42-08:00","id":749062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748458#post748458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Okay, that bit you quoted earlier?<br /> <br /> Did you bother to read the rest of the paragraph?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did actually, but that doesn't add up to any description of &quot;most powerful&quot;, and you don't have to have an attitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The conditions that create a Chamber are on pages 94 and 95. Lingering Chambers stem from encounters with the supernatural traumatic enough to cause actual loss of Integrity. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So much higher probability to become Apex have vampire Sheriff than a Prince - as undead bodyguard dragging or killing people on the streets is much scarier to general humans population than even the most creepy Nosferatu watching them from the sewers. <i>It's all depends on direct impact the monster do on human minds.</i> </div> </div> </div>so, do humans then have to be consciously aware of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T07:17:22-08:00","id":749112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=748112#post748112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (being a programmer) is the Google search engine a single thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The G-M would be more like everything on the internet at once, from google maps, to facebook, to individual blogs, to cooking shows, including all the contradictory parts. Google search engine would be a single Analyst angel and its supporting Infrastructure. Trying to say its only Google search engine (not even all of google at once, but just one small part of the company) is missing the sheer scope and complexity of the G-M. <br /> <br /> Even if we did use your comparison.... point me to the exact location of the google search engine. Not the company headquarters. The search engine itself. You can't. Its code is scattered away in various servers and locations across the globe, as well as every computer running the search engine script remotely as they perform google searches. You are a discrete being with a single location in space. The Internet is a conceptual space that exists simultaneously across the globe<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=749062#post749062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did actually, but that doesn't add up to any description of &quot;most powerful&quot;, and you don't have to have an attitude.<br /> <br /> so, do humans then have to be consciously aware of it?</div> </div> </div> </div> Satchel's quotes really answers your question. It must be a supernatural that interacts with humans regularly, spawns nightmares in the Primordial Dream, and has the largest effect on the local Astral dreamscape.<br /> <br /> Does that have to be consciously aware? No, you don't need to be consciously aware of something to have nightmares about it. The Apex is the all about causing Nightmares. This isn't about a pure match of power. Its about who has the most powerful effect <u><i>on the city's dreamscape</i></u>. <br /> <br /> The Apex is still a Beast thing. Its still all about causing terror and freight. The Primordial Dream doesn't care if an archdemon or freshly awakened mummy is around if people aren't being scared by it. The Primordial Dream is still part of the Onerios, the human consciousness. Everything inside of it has to relate to humanity in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T08:56:54-08:00","id":749241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=749062#post749062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did actually, but that doesn't add up to any description of &quot;most powerful&quot;, and you don't have to have an attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the description of &quot;most powerful&quot; is a fairly incomplete summary based on the tendency of greater supernatural power to come with greater demands for resources and greater risk of exposure does not mean it is sensible to jump immediately to an interpretation that utterly disregards all of that, particularly when it's written on either side of the line you've zoned in on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T18:58:50-08:00","id":750416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/747745-can-the-god-machine-be-the-apex?p=749112#post749112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we did use your comparison.... point me to the exact location of the google search engine. Not the company headquarters. The search engine itself. You can't. Its code is scattered away in various servers and locations across the globe, as well as every computer running the search engine script remotely as they perform google searches. You are a discrete being with a single location in space. The Internet is a conceptual space that exists simultaneously across the globe</div> </div> </div> </div>from a bacteriums perspective we are massive and simply look like cells... it's all systems composed of systems. A single application is composed of data structures and functions, which can be broken down into instructions, and if you're looking at a byte code driven language will be interpreted, etc, etc. How exactly do you propose to distinguish a single entity? Even Google the company is made up of different divisions, and is now (will be?) part of a parent company, and ultimately is made of people, who work within it transiently. When does something become a thing? probably when we can actually define its borders, and I can tell you where the internet begins and ends. Simply because you cannot fathom the size of the Milky Way does not make it less of a discrete thing in the universe, of which we are a very tiny subsystem. Really though this is not a particularly conducive part of the conversation, I'm simply saying that even though the GM is a System of Systems does not make it less of a thing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.htwins.net/scale2/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.htwins.net/scale2/</a> &lt; may help explain what I'm referring to GM and systems wise.<br /> <br /> I can accept the God Machine is beyond the scope of human thinking and thus not eligible. I can also accept that this is about human fear, if even it seems that these few paragraphs aren't particularly great at illustrating that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 11-02-2015, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}